---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../lib/siteConfig";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <Header />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-[28px] font-extrabold tracking-tight text-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mb-10 text-[12.5px] text-text-tertiary">Last updated: REPLACE_ME</p>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is a local-first desktop application. Your bookmarks, folders, tags, notes, and every other
        piece of data you create in the app are stored in a single SQLite database file on your own computer. The
        app does not sync that data to a server, and we do not have access to it.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-[15px] font-bold text-text">What we don't collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
          <li>No bookmark content, titles, URLs, tags, or notes ever leave your device.</li>
          <li>No usage analytics or telemetry are collected by the app.</li>
          <li>No account or sign-up is required to use {siteConfig.name} day to day.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-[15px] font-bold text-text">Sites {siteConfig.name} contacts for you</h2>
        <p>
          A few features contact the websites you've bookmarked, directly from your computer: dead-link checks and feeds
          (only when you ask for them), site icons (which you can switch off in Settings), and saved page copies (only
          for pages you choose, or if you turn on saving new bookmarks automatically). These requests go straight to
          those sites, never through us or a third party, and no bookmark data is sent to us. Adult sites and local
          addresses are never contacted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-[15px] font-bold text-text">Browser extension</h2>
        <p>
          The optional {siteConfig.name} browser extension sends the pages you save to the app on your own computer,
          over a local-only connection that stays off until you turn it on in the app and is protected by a code that
          only you have. Nothing is sent to us or anywhere else. The extension asks your browser only for the
          permissions it needs; if you choose to forward new browser bookmarks it can see bookmarks as you create them,
          and only when you use "Save all tabs" does it read the addresses of your open tabs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-[15px] font-bold text-text">License activation</h2>
        <p>
          Activating a purchased license validates your license key against our payment provider (Lemon Squeezy) to
          confirm it's valid. This exchange includes only what's needed to activate the license — no bookmark data is
          part of it — and the app keeps working during an offline grace period if that check can't reach the
          network.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-[15px] font-bold text-text">This website</h2>
        <p>
          REPLACE_ME — describe any analytics or cookies used by this marketing site itself (e.g. none, or a
          privacy-respecting analytics tool), separately from the desktop app described above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-[15px] font-bold text-text">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can be sent to <a class="text-accent" href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
